  "ab2": {
    "proof": "rarestDf for `bail` was 0.25773984261292154 in ALL EIGHT scopes - unfiltered, one court, and an Allahabad July-2026 window holding 54 documents. The bound was a property of the lexeme alone.",
    "firstAttemptWasWrong": {
      "what": "The bound was first written as rarestDf x population <= maxRankedRows, justified by a hand-written EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) showing 18.204 ms for the 54-document window.",
      "whatHappened": "It admitted the query, and the query then took 10,799 ms.",
      "why": "The hand EXPLAIN inlined to_tsquery('english','bail') as a LITERAL so the planner could cost it and chose judgments_date_court_idx. The real query builds its tsquery inside a CTE from string_agg, so the planner cannot see it and BitmapAnd'd judgments_full_text_idx (4,518,732 rows) against judgments_judgment_date_idx, applying court as a heap filter: 471,836 rows removed by index recheck, 64,527 lossy heap blocks, 2,444,828 buffers.",
      "lesson": "An inlined EXPLAIN is not evidence for a query whose parameters are bound. This repository had already recorded that exact failure once."
    },
    "design": {
      "chosen": "Structured filtering BEFORE lexical ranking (candidate 1) + a cheap capped filtered-population probe (candidate 3). The probe admits; a MATERIALIZED fence guarantees the plan.",
      "rejected": {
        "a per-court/month counts table": "coverage_cell exists but is court x YEAR and its `held` was measured 19 August. Admission would depend on a stale artifact owned by a different concern, and a month-scoped query would be judged on a year.",
        "ask the planner via EXPLAIN": "a second parse per request, returning an estimate this file has already measured as wrong by 200x (rows=84744 against 16,965,472).",
        "drop the guard and rely on statement_timeout": "that is the site-stall behaviour, re-bought.",
        "ParadeDB / a semantic router": "excluded by the round."
      },
      "boundDerivation": "Cost is per ELIGIBLE row, not per matched row, because every eligible row must have its tsvector read to test @@. Measured filter-first: 54 rows/12ms, 5,489/1,363ms, 12,827/3,503ms = 0.22, 0.248, 0.27 ms per eligible row. FILTERED_MAX_ELIGIBLE_ROWS = 5,000ms budget / 0.25ms = 20,000, against CORE_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS 10,000.",
      "sargability": "The probe and the fence use judgment_date range predicates, never date_part(year, ...), so judgments_date_court_idx stays usable. No ILIKE is introduced where an indexed identifier exists."
    },
